"# Research Session Established ✅\n\n**Smoke test passed.** The English Wikipedia source is reachable through the search pipeline and returning verifiable, citable results. Session is ready to accept a factual question.\n\n---\n\n## Session Configuration\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Primary source** | English Wikipedia (`en.wikipedia.org`) only |\n| **Search scope** | Site-restricted queries (`site:en.wikipedia.org`) |\n| **Language** | English |\n| **Citation format** | Numbered references `[1]`, `[2]`, … with article titles + canonical URLs |\n| **Verification** | Live smoke test completed 2026-09-26 |\n\n## Operating Protocol for This Session\n\n1. **Source discipline** — Every factual claim in answers will be grounded in English Wikipedia article content retrieved via search, never from memory alone.\n2. **Citation standard** — Each answer carries numbered citations mapping to specific Wikipedia articles and URLs.\n3. **Freshness handling** — Where Wikipedia content is dynamic (article counts, statistics, current-officeholder infoboxes), the answer will note that figures reflect the latest indexed snapshot and may have changed since.\n4. **Coverage strategy** — Multi-faceted questions will be decomposed into 2–5 focused subtopic searches run in parallel, all against English Wikipedia.\n5. **Transparency** — If a fact cannot be verified on English Wikipedia (or coverage is thin/contested), the answer will say so explicitly rather than filling gaps from outside the source.\n\n## Smoke-Test Result (Verification Record)\n\nThe test query against the English Wikipedia article **\"Wikipedia\"** returned correctly attributed, citable content:\n- Launched **January 15, 2001** by Jimmy Wales and Larry Sanger [1]\n- Operated by the **Wikimedia Foundation**, a U.S. nonprofit [1]\n- English Wikipedia holds **7+ million articles** (7-million milestone passed November 2024); all editions combined exceed **60 million** [1][2]\n\nThis confirms the pipeline resolves English Wikipedia articles, extracts facts, and produces source-linked citations as configured.\n\n---\n\n**Session is live.** Submit the factual question to be answered; it will be researched exclusively against English Wikipedia and returned with full citations."